IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rta-restraints`

-- Restraints of Trade Act 1976 (NSW) -- worked cases for every exported question in rta-restraints.l4.
-- Every expected value was worked by hand from the deposited text; none was copied from the encoding's output. Each
-- assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Dates are illustrative.
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `cases`

GIVEN dd IS A NUMBER, mm IS A NUMBER, yy IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`d` dd mm yy MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY dd mm yy

-- The running example: an employee whose employment ended on 30 June 2026, bound by a 12-month non-compete from
-- 1 July 2026 to 30 June 2027; a court would find six months (to 31 December 2026) the most that is not against public
-- policy.
`begins` MEANS `d` 1 7 2026
`written last day` MEANS `d` 30 6 2027
`six months` MEANS `d` 31 12 2026

`contract` MEANS `by a contract`
`association rules` MEANS `by the rules of an association I am a member of`
`other way` MEANS `in some other way`
`creator` MEANS `a person who created the restraint or joined in creating it`
`association` MEANS `the association whose rules bind me as a member`
`stranger` MEANS `someone who neither created it nor joined in creating it`
`nobody` MEANS `nobody: the Court finds no manifest failure`

§§ `s 3 -- does the Act apply`

-- Arguments: created before assent; contract says the Act does not apply; another law.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` FALSE FALSE `no other law` EQUALS `The Act applies to my restraint`
-- s 3(2): a stipulation to the contrary changes nothing.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` FALSE TRUE `no other law` EQUALS `The Act applies to my restraint`
-- s 3(3): the other laws run beside the Act.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` FALSE FALSE `section 304 of the Industrial Relations Act 1996` EQUALS `The Act applies, and the other law named also operates: the Act does not affect it`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` FALSE TRUE `section 125 of the Co-operatives National Law (NSW)` EQUALS `The Act applies, and the other law named also operates: the Act does not affect it`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` FALSE FALSE `another enactment about the validity of a restraint of trade` EQUALS `The Act applies, and the other law named also operates: the Act does not affect it`
-- s 3(1): created before assent.
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` TRUE FALSE `no other law` EQUALS `The Act does not apply: my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`
#ASSERT `Does the Act apply to my restraint` TRUE TRUE `section 304 of the Industrial Relations Act 1996` EQUALS `The Act does not apply: my restraint was created before the date of assent to the Act`

§§ `s 4(1), (2) -- how far valid`

-- Arguments: before assent; invalid for another reason; how much against public policy; severable.
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE FALSE `none of it` FALSE EQUALS `It is valid: no part of it is against public policy`
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE FALSE `part of it` FALSE EQUALS `It is valid only to the extent it is not against public policy (read down), whether or not it is in severable terms`
-- "whether it is in severable terms or not": the same answer.
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE FALSE `part of it` TRUE EQUALS `It is valid only to the extent it is not against public policy (read down), whether or not it is in severable terms`
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE FALSE `all of it` TRUE EQUALS `It is not valid: all of it is against public policy`
-- s 4(2): another invalidity stands, whatever public policy says.
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE TRUE `none of it` FALSE EQUALS `It is invalid for a reason other than public policy, which the Act leaves alone`
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` FALSE TRUE `part of it` TRUE EQUALS `It is invalid for a reason other than public policy, which the Act leaves alone`
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` TRUE FALSE `part of it` FALSE EQUALS `The Act does not apply: the general law decides`
#ASSERT `How far is my restraint valid` TRUE TRUE `none of it` FALSE EQUALS `The Act does not apply: the general law decides`

§§ `s 4(1) -- until what day`

-- Arguments: before assent; invalid for another reason; how much; written last day; last day not against policy.
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `It binds me up to and including` (`d` 31 12 2026)
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `none of it` `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `It binds me up to and including` (`d` 30 6 2027)
-- Only the area too wide: the court's last day is the written one, or later; the written period still caps it.
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `written last day` (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS `It binds me up to and including` (`d` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `written last day` (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS `It binds me up to and including` (`d` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `written last day` (`d` 29 6 2027) EQUALS `It binds me up to and including` (`d` 29 6 2027)
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE FALSE `all of it` `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `It does not bind me at all`
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` FALSE TRUE `none of it` `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `It does not bind me at all`
#ASSERT `Until what day does my restraint bind me` TRUE FALSE `part of it` `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `The Act does not decide this: the general law does`

§§ `s 4(3) -- can I apply`

-- Arguments: subject to the restraint; before assent.
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can I apply to the Supreme Court about my restraint` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 4(3), (4) -- can the Court make an order`

-- Arguments: subject; before assent; how created; how much as regards me; whose failure; at least partly because of it.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `all of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `other way` `part of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- "against public policy to any extent" fails.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `none of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- "by reason of, or partly by reason of" fails.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The failure is not a creator's, or there is none.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `stranger` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `all of it` `nobody` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- s 4(4): the association is deemed a creator for a restraint under its rules on a member.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `association rules` `part of it` `association` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Not under its rules: s 4(4) does not deem, and the Act does not answer (fork F3).
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `association` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `other way` `all of it` `association` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not the applicant, or before assent.
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` FALSE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE TRUE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Can the Supreme Court make an order about my restraint` TRUE TRUE `association rules` `all of it` `association` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `s 4(3) -- what the Court may order`

-- Arguments: as above, then the written last day and the last day not against public policy.
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `That my restraint is altogether invalid, or valid as regards me up to a day no later than` (`d` 31 12 2026)
-- Area too wide only: the cap is the written last day.
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE `written last day` (`d` 31 12 2027) EQUALS `That my restraint is altogether invalid, or valid as regards me up to a day no later than` (`d` 30 6 2027)
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `association rules` `all of it` `association` TRUE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `Only that my restraint is altogether invalid as regards me`
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` FALSE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `none of it` `creator` TRUE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` TRUE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `association` TRUE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`
#ASSERT `What may the Court order about my restraint` FALSE FALSE `contract` `part of it` `creator` TRUE `written last day` `six months` EQUALS `The Court has no power under section 4(3) on these facts`

§§ `s 4(3) -- when the order takes effect`

-- Arguments: the day the order was made; the day it says it takes effect.
#ASSERT `From what day does the Court's order take effect` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 1 10 2026)
#ASSERT `From what day does the Court's order take effect` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST (`d` 15 10 2026)
-- One day earlier than the order: barred ("not being a date earlier"); the Act does not say what follows (fork F4).
#ASSERT `From what day does the Court's order take effect` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `From what day does the Court's order take effect` (`d` 1 1 2027) (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `s 4(5) -- accrued rights`

-- Arguments: order made; takes effect; the day the right accrued.
#ASSERT `Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 10 2026) (`d` 14 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- On the day the order takes effect, or after: outside s 4(5).
#ASSERT `Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 10 2026) (`d` 20 10 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Does the Court's order take away a right already accrued against me` (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) (`d` 1 9 2026) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `Would doing it on this day break my restraint`

-- Arguments, in order: before assent; invalid for another reason; how much; begins; written last day; last day not
-- against policy; what I do is within the valid part; an order made; order made on; order takes effect; order makes it
-- altogether invalid; order's last valid day; within what the order leaves valid; the day I do it.
-- No order: s 4(1) reads the 12 months down to six (to 31 December 2026).
`no order` MEANS `d` 1 1 2000

#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 30 6 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside the part not against public policy (for example a customer the restraint could not reasonably cover).
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` FALSE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- None of it against public policy: the full written period.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `none of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` FALSE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `none of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- All of it against public policy: binds on no day.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `all of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Invalid for another reason (fork F2); before assent (NOTHING).
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE TRUE `none of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` TRUE FALSE `none of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 8 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Area too wide only: the written period stands, even if the court's day is later.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` (`d` 31 12 2027) TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 30 6 2027) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` (`d` 31 12 2027) TRUE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 7 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- An order made and taking effect on 1 October 2026 that the restraint is altogether invalid as regards me: a breach on
-- 30 September is still a breach (s 4(5), s 4(1) governs before the order); on 1 October it is not.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) TRUE `no order` FALSE (`d` 30 9 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) TRUE `no order` FALSE (`d` 1 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order leaving it valid to 30 November 2026.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 30 11 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 1 12 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Outside what the order leaves valid.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 30 11 2026) FALSE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order purporting to leave it valid to 31 March 2027: capped at 31 December 2026 ("not exceeding").
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 31 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 31 12 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 31 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 1 1 2027) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order leaving valid an activity that s 4(1) does not (fork F8, "not exceeding"): no breach, as with no order.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` FALSE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 30 11 2026) TRUE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` FALSE FALSE `no order` `no order` FALSE `no order` FALSE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- All of it against public policy: an order cannot revive it.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `all of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 1 10 2026) FALSE (`d` 31 3 2027) TRUE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- An order specifying a day earlier than it was made (fork F4).
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 30 9 2026) TRUE `no order` FALSE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The order takes effect later than made (15 October): s 4(1) governs until then.
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 10 2026) TRUE `no order` FALSE (`d` 14 10 2026) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Would doing it on this day break my restraint` FALSE FALSE `part of it` `begins` `written last day` `six months` TRUE TRUE (`d` 1 10 2026) (`d` 15 10 2026) TRUE `no order` FALSE (`d` 15 10 2026) EQUALS JUST FALSE
